    "relaxation_hazard": {
      "statement": "Unlike a new optional field, relaxing an existing MUST makes previously-INVALID documents valid. An L1 reader written against today's text may reject a name-only GeoLocation outright rather than degrade.",
      "why_it_may_still_be_fine": "The spec already establishes a writer-strict / reader-lenient asymmetry (value resolution CA-003, version stamping, unknown dot-prefixed members). This relaxation fits that pattern if readers are directed to render what they have and not reject.",
      "what_this_seat_does_NOT_claim": "That the asymmetry obviously covers it. A reader that cannot plot a point is in a different position from a reader ignoring an unknown key, and that distinction is the spec org's to draw."
    },
